From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 23:07:26 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 36/67] Meridian: Chromium's bubbles in the WebUI window
 (permissions, multiple downloads, save password)

There's no toolbar or location bar: the stub location bar reports itself
not drawn, so permission requests are bubbles (not chips or quiet icons
nobody sees, which silently denied location asked on load); the password
bubble anchors like page info; anchoring no longer dereferences a missing
BrowserView (crashed on a permission prompt with the location icon hidden).
Tests list and answer the bubbles through --meridian-test-bubbles.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
